{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDssi1dczYxxi89QwAh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it in `money.py:5-6`. The function was rounding every share down and throwing away the leftover grosze. Now it adds one grosz to each of the first `remainder` shares:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1] * remainder + [share] * (people - remainder)\n```\n\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`. I also checked it against 101/3, 5/7, 0/2, 1/1 and a negative total (-100/3). Each time the shares added up to the full total and differed by at most 1. The 3 existing tests still pass.\n\nTwo things to know before deploying:\n- **Who pays the extra grosz:** the first people in the list always get it. If something downstream expects the shares in a fixed order, check that it's fine with this.\n- **Not committed:** the change is only in your working tree, ready for you to commit and push in the deploy window. A regression test is a single line, `self.assertEqual(split_cents(100, 3), [34, 33, 33])`, if you want to add it next sprint."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":799,"cache_read_input_tokens":18133,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":799},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feac23e7-fcf1-4f25-8e7d-dde3fec6204b","uuid":"3b59ec25-e135-4b82-80d9-a8523c40a20e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:22:03.128Z","request_id":"req_011CggDssEjnqQTKK5RMA2Fm"}
